    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Present design evidence shows no untrusted source reaches a sensitive sink today: the requester is trusted, docs.search is read only, replies are bound to the authenticated requester, and there is no external network egress. The roadmap introduces significant change triggers: adding web.fetch and a Jira MCP server with customer-authored tickets would create an untrusted-content source that can influence confidential retrieval and an irreversible reply path. The only declared content safeguard is behavioral prompt text, so the forecast rises to critical if those changes are made without structural isolation and sink constraints. Manual validation was applied because scripts could not be run."
